1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,114
Welcome to Night 4.

2
00:00:02,064 --> 00:00:11,300
Tonight we shape the cave, your physical sleep environment, into a place your brain learns to associate exclusively with rest.

3
00:00:11,300 --> 00:00:13,608
The science is precise.

4
00:00:13,608 --> 00:00:20,167
Your core body temperature must drop by about one to two degrees Celsius for sleep to begin.

5
00:00:20,167 --> 00:00:26,888
If your bedroom is warm, your body cannot release that heat, and sleep onset is delayed.

6
00:00:26,888 --> 00:00:32,417
Studies converge on a sweet spot of sixteen to nineteen degrees Celsius.

7
00:00:32,417 --> 00:00:35,535
Cooler than feels comfortable when you walk in.

8
00:00:35,535 --> 00:00:38,138
Warm only under the covers.

9
00:00:38,138 --> 00:00:40,549
Light is just as critical.

10
00:00:40,549 --> 00:00:50,976
Even small amounts of light, including the standby LED on a TV or the glow of a charger, signal to your brain that morning is approaching.

11
00:00:50,976 --> 00:00:54,064
Melatonin production stays suppressed.

12
00:00:54,064 --> 00:00:56,020
Sleep stays shallow.

13
00:00:56,020 --> 00:01:01,711
Sound matters less than most people think, but consistency matters more.

14
00:01:01,711 --> 00:01:08,402
A steady fan or white noise is far better than a quiet room with occasional disruptions.

15
00:01:08,402 --> 00:01:12,932
Your brain monitors for changes, not absolute volume.

16
00:01:12,932 --> 00:01:16,182
So tonight, make four adjustments.

17
00:01:16,182 --> 00:01:17,667
Cool the room.

18
00:01:17,667 --> 00:01:21,564
Block out every source of light, including window light.

19
00:01:21,564 --> 00:01:25,388
Remove any light-emitting device from your line of sight.

20
00:01:25,388 --> 00:01:33,152
And add a constant low hum, a fan or noise machine, if your room has unpredictable sounds.

21
00:01:33,152 --> 00:01:36,344
Your bed is now a place that does one thing.

22
00:01:36,344 --> 00:01:38,152
It signals sleep.

23
00:01:38,152 --> 00:01:39,917
Let your eyes close.

24
00:01:39,917 --> 00:01:41,799
Let your face soften.

25
00:01:41,799 --> 00:01:44,711
Notice the weight of your body against the bed.

26
00:01:44,711 --> 00:01:47,917
Breathe in slowly for four seconds.

27
00:01:47,917 --> 00:01:49,520
Hold for seven.

28
00:01:49,520 --> 00:01:51,152
Release for eight.

29
00:01:51,152 --> 00:01:52,329
Again.

30
00:01:52,329 --> 00:01:53,799
In for four.

31
00:01:53,799 --> 00:01:55,402
Hold for seven.

32
00:01:55,402 --> 00:01:56,770
Out for eight.

33
00:01:56,770 --> 00:01:58,167
Last time.

34
00:01:58,167 --> 00:01:59,638
In for four.

35
00:01:59,638 --> 00:02:01,241
Hold for seven.

36
00:02:01,241 --> 00:02:02,608
Out for eight.

37
00:02:02,608 --> 00:02:04,417
The cave is dark.

38
00:02:04,417 --> 00:02:06,094
The cave is cool.

39
00:02:06,094 --> 00:02:07,432
Sleep well.

